Cases: SDDPurpose:  Case specifications define WHAT needs to be built.  Each case is a project instance with its own tech stack,  dependencies, and execution chain.Owns: ./ReadOrder:   1  @INDEX.sdd   2  @payment-integration.sdd   3  @microservices-migration.sdd   4  @real-time-analytics.sdd   5  @mobile-banking-app.sdd   6  @ecommerce-platform.sddModes:  EXECUTE  — execute the case  REVIEW   — review case status  PLAN     — plan case execution  AUDIT    — audit case driftRules:  [C1] Cases MUST have unique IDs.  [C2] Cases MUST define dependencies.  [C3] Cases MUST specify tech_stack.  [C4] Cases MUST have approval_required gates.  [C5] Cases MUST define provisioning triggers.  [C6] State transitions MUST be recorded.  [C7] Cases MUST NOT be executed without human approval for architectural decisions.Entry:  Read:    INDEX.sdd  Resolve:    payment-integration    microservices-migration    real-time-analytics    mobile-banking-app    ecommerce-platformNavigation:  Cases: @cases/INDEX.sdd  PaymentIntegration: @cases/payment-integration.sdd  MicroservicesMigration: @cases/microservices-migration.sdd  RealTimeAnalytics: @cases/real-time-analytics.sdd  MobileBankingApp: @cases/mobile-banking-app.sdd  EcommercePlatform: @cases/ecommerce-platform.sddState: +
